Two four-band elementary band representations, and whether their bands can
be separated: SG 199 (Flicker et al., PRB 98, 155145) and SG 208 (Cano et
al., PRL 120, 266401).
Bands are counted from 0, as pythtb counts them.

1. SG 199: the group, and the levels of the four bands
   realized group   : #199.13 I2_131', s orbitals at Wyckoff 8a, 4 bands
   GM               : GM4(3) at -1.000000, GM1(1) at +3.000000
   H                : H1(1) at -3.000000, H4(3) at +1.000000
   N                : N1(1) at -2.236068, N2(1) at -1.000000, N2(1) at +1.000000, N1(1) at +2.236068
   P                : P1(2) at -1.732051, P3(2) at +1.732051
   PA               : PA1(2) at -1.732051, PA3(2) at +1.732051
   GM4 and H4 are threefold: the spin-1 fermions

2. SG 199: the four bands together, and the three inter-band gaps
   all 4 bands      : GM1 + GM4 + H1 + H4 + 2×N1 + 2×N2 + P1 + P3 + PA1 + PA3
   atomic limit     : 1 x A1↑G(4)@8a(31',3)
   bands 0 and 1    : smallest direct gap 0.000000 over a 13x13x13 mesh
   bands 1 and 2    : smallest direct gap 0.000000
   bands 2 and 3    : smallest direct gap 0.000000
   every gap closes somewhere, so no subset of the four bands is isolated at any
   filling: this elementary band representation is connected

3. SG 208: the group, the crystal field the paper draws, and the levels
   realized group   : #208.45 P4_2321', orbitals at Wyckoff 2a, 4 bands
   crystal field    : 24 atoms that carry no orbital, the paper's own device
   GM               : GM3(2) at -0.861626, GM3(2) at +0.861626
   M                : M5(2) at -0.258199, M5(2) at +0.258199
   R                : R3(2) at -1.200000, R3(2) at +1.200000
   X                : X5(2) at -0.258199, X5(2) at +0.258199

4. SG 208: the four bands together, and the three inter-band gaps
   all 4 bands      : 2×GM3 + 2×M5 + 2×R3 + 2×X5
   atomic limit     : 1 x 1E2E↑G(4)@2a(231',23)
   bands 0 and 1    : smallest direct gap 0.000000 over a 13x13x13 mesh
   bands 1 and 2    : smallest direct gap 0.256971
   bands 2 and 3    : smallest direct gap 0.000000
   half filling     : indirect gap 0.256971
   the gap between bands 1 and 2 stays open, so this elementary band representation
   splits at half filling into two isolated halves of two bands each

5. SG 208: each half of the split on its own
   bands 0 and 1    : GM3 + M5 + R3 + X5
   atomic limits    : none
   bands 2 and 3    : GM3 + M5 + R3 + X5
   atomic limits    : none
   each isolated half is topological

6. the bands of both models, one panel each

